Substrate
================================================================================
Forbric is built on Fabric Loader, which is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

    Fabric Loader
    Copyright 2016 FabricMC
    https://github.com/FabricMC/fabric-loader

THIS REPOSITORY CONTAINS NO FABRIC LOADER SOURCE CODE. The substrate is a
separate checkout of the upstream repository above, at the release pinned as
`fabric_loader_ref` in forbric-loader/gradle.properties (0.19.3): bootstrap.sh
fetches it into a sibling directory, and forbric-loader/build.gradle compiles
its source roots alongside Forbric's own. Nothing here is therefore a file
"derived from Fabric Loader", and no file in this repository carries a FabricMC
copyright header.

What this repository does carry is the set of changes Forbric needs in that
upstream code: the patches under forbric-loader/patches/fabric-loader/. They are
unified diffs against the pinned release, so they quote short excerpts of
upstream's source as context; those excerpts remain Copyright FabricMC under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

The BUILT jar is a different matter from this repository. Because the substrate
is compiled into it, forbric-loader-<version>.jar contains compiled Apache-2.0
Fabric Loader code, Copyright FabricMC, which retains upstream's copyright and
is redistributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Anyone redistributing
the built jar is redistributing that code and must carry this NOTICE with it.

================================================================================
Forge-side code: clean-room
================================================================================
Forbric's Forge-compatibility code (the net.forbric.loader.impl.*.forge.*
packages and related Forge metadata / mapping / access / lifecycle code) is an
independent clean-room implementation written from public formats and
specifications (the mods.toml schema, JarInJar metadata, modern Forge
IEventBus/registry contracts, the Maven version-range grammar, and Mixin).

It does NOT contain any source code from Forge Mod Loader (FML). FML, which is
licensed under the GNU LGPL v2.1 or later, was consulted only as a behavioural
reference. See CREDITS.md.

The MinecraftForge and NeoForge runtimes themselves are not redistributed here
either: they are fetched and assembled at run time by the scripts under
forbric-loader/run/, and loaded from the user's own machine.

================================================================================
Mappings
================================================================================
Forbric does NOT bundle MCP mapping data, which is non-redistributable.
Runtime mappings are generated from permitted sources only (Mojang official
mappings, Fabric intermediary, and Yarn). See MAPPINGS.md.

